  "verdict": "Across 12 instruments the median funding settlement is exactly zero on 12 of them, 81% of all settlements pay nothing, and 12 settle negative less than 5% of the time \u2014 funding here is one-sided and sparse, so a mean is a tail statistic and carries a bootstrap interval rather than being annualised on its own. Of 3 delta-neutral baskets, 3 have a funding rate whose 95% interval excludes zero \u2014 and that is the number this study exists to distrust. **short 1.000 QQQUSDT + long 0.328 TQQQUSDT is a carry that loses money.** It pays +3.94% a year in funding with an interval clear of zero, and held through the real series over 14-day windows it returns -0.082%, positive in only 24% of them: the funding arrives (+0.160%) and the price leg gives back more (-0.123%). A funding table alone would have recommended precisely this trade, which is why there is a replay. 2 of 3 pay when actually held. The best is short 1.000 TQQQUSDT + short 0.969 SQQQUSDT at +0.221% per 14-day hold net of its 24bps round trip, positive in 74% of 1823 overlapping windows \u2014 which is about 6 independent holds, not 1823, and the win rate should be read against that. **It should not be called a carry.** Only 21% of that return is funding (+0.046%); the rest is the price leg (+0.295%), which for a basket short both a leveraged token and its inverse is volatility decay. That is a short-gamma position \u2014 74%-style win rates with a -3.30% worst window are the shape of one \u2014 and selling it as funding carry would misdescribe both the source of the return and the risk being run. 5.0% of the basket's variance is unhedged, and that residual is what the position is actually paid for bearing."
